    "theorem_export": {
      "claim": "On five-node supports in Z12, any full-Aut unit-band pair action that weights distance-1 and distance-5 unit bands equally cannot derive the P2370 distance-5 band-pass selector. The Aut-invariant score h1+h5 is maximized by 24 mixed supports with (h1,h5)=(3,3), not by the 12 distance-5 paths with (0,4). For scores a*h1+b*h5 with b>0 and a>=0, the distance-5 path orbit is uniquely selected only in the symmetry-breaking chamber a/b<1/3. Thus the band-pass polarity is an extra selector/source premise unless bridge-completed dynamics exports it.",
